; The language servers and `dune` itself are invisible to dune's dependency
; tracking: nothing in the build graph changes when gopls or rust-analyzer is
; upgraded, so a cached green result outlives the toolchain it was produced
; with. `servers.version` closes that hole by recording what is actually
; installed and making the test depend on the recording.
;
; (universe) is what makes the probe re-run on every build — it is dune's marker
; for "this action reads the outside world". The probe itself is three version
; calls; when the output is byte-identical, dune still caches the test, so the
; cost is the probe and not the suite.
;
; Absence is recorded, not fatal: a machine without rust-analyzer writes
; "rust-analyzer: absent" and the tests take their own skip path (or fail under
; ARCH_TEZT_REQUIRE_SERVERS=1, which is that flag's job, not this rule's).
(rule
 (target servers.version)
 (deps (universe))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{target}
   (progn
    ; The probe is captured first and defaulted, rather than piped into an `||`:
    ; in `prog | head -1 || echo absent` the exit status is HEAD's, which is 0
    ; whatever prog did, so a missing tool recorded as a blank field instead of
    ; "absent" — and a blank field still differs from the next machine's blank
    ; field only by luck.
    (run sh -c "v=$(gopls version 2>/dev/null | head -1); printf 'gopls: %s\n' \"${v:-absent}\"")
    (run sh -c "v=$(rust-analyzer --version 2>/dev/null); printf 'rust-analyzer: %s\n' \"${v:-absent}\"")
    (run sh -c "v=$(typescript-language-server --version 2>/dev/null); printf 'typescript-language-server: %s\n' \"${v:-absent}\"")
    (run sh -c "v=$(dune --version 2>/dev/null); printf 'dune: %s\n' \"${v:-absent}\"")))))

; These `deps` attach to the `runtest` ALIAS, not to building `main.exe` as a file target --
; that is dune's own semantics for a `(test)` stanza. Measured in this worktree (2026-09-06, base 6930d3c):
; after `dune clean`, `dune build --root . tezt/tests/main.exe` produced `main.exe` and left
; `_build/default/bin` with 0 `.exe` files.
;
; The executables are pulled in from elsewhere instead: `tezt/lib/dune`'s `cli_paths.ml` rule
; lists them as its `deps`, and `arch_tezt.ml` references the generated module. Same
; clean-then-scoped-build procedure after adding that rule: 19 of the 19 executables it lists
; present. An earlier text here and in docs/mutation-testing.md said no stanza-level fix
; existed; issue #77's second comment refuted it with the prototype that rule is built from.
;
; FOUND-VS-NAMED on that refuted premise. `git grep "dune exec tezt/tests/main.exe"` and
; `git grep "does NOT rebuild a test"`, over ALL tracked files rather than just `.md`
; (2026-09-06), find it at FIVE further live sites across four files. Each now carries a
; superseding note. Four are fully superseded; the fifth only PARTLY, because for
; `test/<t>.exe` nothing changed:
;   specs/point-free-aliases.md:349
;   specs/qualified-unit-resolution.md:314  (its `tezt/tests/dune:35-36` coordinate is stale)
;   specs/qualified-unit-resolution.md:377
;   specs/reexport-resolution.md:535
;   scripts/mutate-check.sh:9-11  (the script's design rationale; PARTLY superseded only)
; Their in-session demonstrations were accurate for the trees they ran on; the premise is what
; changed. `briefs/` (8 lines, 7 files) was left alone as history. Line citations INTO the files
; this commit edits were also left alone outside specs/: 10 in roster/, 5 in briefs/.
;
; INVOCATIONS.
;
; Whole suite: `dune build --root=.` (full) then `dune runtest`, or `dune runtest` alone. Both
; work; at merge-base "`dune runtest` alone" was not true, and the rule above is what makes it so.
;
; One test, which is what a mutation run needs: run the binary directly. `dune runtest` cannot be
; scoped -- `dune runtest -- --file X` is refused ("--file does not match any known test") and
; `dune build @runtest -- --file X` is refused ("Don't know how to build --file").
;   dune build --root=.
;   ./_build/default/tezt/tests/main.exe --file <file>.ml --keep-going
; Measured: `--file tezt/tests/helpers.ml --keep-going` gave `(1/2)`, `(2/2)`, exit 0. That form
; reads no dune stanza, so nothing edited here can change it, and `--keep-going` is passed
; explicitly because the `(action)` field below belongs to the `runtest` alias.
;
; The earlier text here read "NEVER `dune exec tezt/tests/main.exe` or a scoped
; `dune build tezt/tests/main.exe`", on the ground that a scoped build leaves the CLIs unbuilt.
; The rule above removes that ground: the executables are deps of COMPILING `arch_tezt`, so they
; exist before `main.exe` is linked. Measured as a pair, neither half meaning much alone -- after
; `dune clean`, a scoped `dune build --root . tezt/tests/main.exe` left 19 `.exe` under
; `_build/default/bin` and `_build/default/poc` (0 at merge-base), and
; `dune exec --root=. tezt/tests/main.exe -- --keep-going`
; on that tree gave exit 0, `(227/227)`. Recorded as safe, not as recommended; the two forms above
; are the recommended ones. One measured difference on that route:
; `_build/default/tezt/tests/servers.version` is not produced by a scoped build and did not exist
; during that run. No `.ml` under `tezt/` reads it; it is a `deps` entry of the stanza below.
;
; See docs/mutation-testing.md, "Scoping a run to one test", which carries the same three forms.
(test
 (name main)
 (libraries arch_tezt tezt arch_index arch_tools sqlite3)
 ; Without this field, `dune test` runs `main.exe` with no arguments and the suite stops at the
 ; first failing case, so a red run reports a lower bound on the failure set. The played count
 ; is carried in each line's `(N/M)` prefix; the runs recorded below print no summary line.
 ;
 ; A/B on one tree (2026-09-06, base 6930d3c), two deliberately failing cases registered ahead of
 ; the other 227, the field being the only difference:
 ;   field absent  -> `(1/229, 1 failed)`,   1 FAILURE line,  exit 1
 ;   field present -> `(229/229, 2 failed)`, 2 FAILURE lines, exit 1
 ;
 ; Green run on this tree with the field: `(227/227)`, exit 0.
 ;
 ; The other side of the trade, three measurements: `main.exe --help` lists `--keep-going, -k`
 ; and no `--no-keep-going`; `dune runtest -- <args>` is refused; `dune build @runtest -- <args>`
 ; is refused. So for `dune runtest` this field is unconditional, and every red `dune runtest`
 ; now plays all 227 cases rather than stopping at the first. Running the binary directly (see
 ; INVOCATIONS above) reads no stanza and is the route that takes different flags.
 ;
 ; Positive control that the field is applied rather than silently ignored:
 ; `dune runtest --display=verbose` printed
 ; `Running[19]: (cd _build/default/tezt/tests && ./main.exe --keep-going)`.
 (action
  (run %{test} --keep-going))
 (deps
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_callgraph_ocaml/arch_callgraph_ocaml.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_query/arch_query.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_index_cli/arch_index_cli.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_load/arch_load.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_body_compare/arch_body_compare.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_coverage_load/arch_coverage_load.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_curate/arch_curate.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_coverage/arch_coverage.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_serve/arch_serve.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_rules/arch_rules.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_report/arch_report.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_sarif_load/arch_sarif_load.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_impact/arch_impact.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_coverage_matrix/arch_coverage_matrix.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_callgraph_rust_merge/arch_callgraph_rust_merge.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_effects_ocaml/arch_effects_ocaml.exe}
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_effects_load/main.exe}
  ../../effects-schema-migration.sql
  %{exe:../../bin/arch_mutants/arch_mutants.exe}
  %{exe:../../poc/decision-lint/bin/decision_lint.exe}
  ../../architecture-schema.sql
  ../../checks/origin-recurring-consumer.js
  ../../scripts/origin-consumer.js
  ../../scripts/origin-consumer-artifacts.js
  ../../test/fixtures/origin-consumer/consumer.ml
